SUPREME PEOPLE'S COURT

Notice on Issuing the "Implementation Measures of the People's Courts for the 'Provisions on the Recording, Reporting, and Accountability for Leading Cadres Interfering in Judicial Activities or Intervening in the Handling of Specific Cases'"

Fa Fa [2015] No. 10

To the High People's Courts of all provinces, autonomous regions, and municipalities directly under the Central Government; the Military Court of the People's Liberation Army; the Production and Construction Corps Branch of the High People's Court of the Xinjiang Uygur Autonomous Region:

The "Implementation Measures of the People's Courts for the 'Provisions on the Recording, Reporting, and Accountability for Leading Cadres Interfering in Judicial Activities or Intervening in the Handling of Specific Cases'" are hereby issued for implementation, effective from August 20, 2015. Please conscientiously implement and enforce them, and ensure the submission for filing of implementation rules and regular reports on implementation status. Any issues discovered during implementation shall be promptly reported to the Supreme People's Court.

August 19, 2015

Implementation Measures of the People's Courts for the "Provisions on the Recording, Reporting, and Accountability for Leading Cadres Interfering in Judicial Activities or Intervening in the Handling of Specific Cases"

To implement the "Provisions on the Recording, Reporting, and Accountability for Leading Cadres Interfering in Judicial Activities or Intervening in the Handling of Specific Cases" (Document No. 23 (2015) of the General Office of the CPC Central Committee, hereinafter referred to as the "Provisions") issued by the General Office of the CPC Central Committee and the General Office of the State Council, and to ensure that the People's Courts independently and impartially exercise their adjudicative power in accordance with the law, these Measures are formulated in light of the actual work of the courts.

Article 1 People's Courts shall independently and impartially exercise their adjudicative power in accordance with the Constitution and the law, free from interference by administrative organs, social organizations, or individuals. They shall not execute any demands made by any organization or individual that violate statutory duties or statutory procedures or hinder judicial justice.

Article 2 Where an organization or individual other than a People's Court transmits correspondence, letters, or oral opinions involving a specific case outside the litigation proceedings, the personnel of the People's Court shall comprehensively, truthfully, and promptly record such matters, and retain the relevant materials, ensuring full documentation, permanent storage, and verifiability.

Where a leading cadre makes a request to a People's Court regarding the handling of a case in an individual capacity or on behalf of an organization, or where staff members or relatives working for a leading cadre interfere in judicial activities or intervene in the handling of a specific case, the People's Court shall record such matters and retain the relevant materials.

Article 3 People's Courts shall, relying on information technology, establish a dedicated database for information on inquiries made by external persons within the case information management system, and clearly define the procedures and authorities for entering, storing, transmitting, viewing, and processing relevant information. When information on inquiries by external persons is entered into the case information management system, it shall be simultaneously entered into the dedicated database for information on inquiries by external persons. The specialized trial management body of the People's Court shall be responsible for the maintenance and management of the dedicated database.

Article 4 When fulfilling the recording obligation under Article 2 of these Measures, personnel of the People's Court shall truthfully record the name, unit, and position of the relevant person, as well as the time, content, and form of the incoming document or communication. For inquiries made through mobile phone text messages, microblogs, WeChat, email, or other online information methods, the storage medium of the information shall also be recorded. For oral inquiries regarding a specific case, the location of occurrence and persons present shall also be recorded, and other personnel of the People's Court present shall sign for confirmation.

The above records and related correspondence, letters, audiovisual materials, electronic data, etc., shall be entered and stored by category. Written materials shall be attached to the case file and archived for future reference; for other materials, the location of their storage shall be indicated at the time of archiving.

Article 5 Where a Party or government organ, industry association or chamber of commerce, social welfare organization, or public institution legally undertaking administrative functions, upon commission or permission by the People's Court, submits reference opinions in accordance with working procedures regarding cases involving national interests or public interests, such opinions may not be entered into the dedicated database for information on inquiries by external persons, but the relevant materials shall be placed in the main case file for future reference.

Article 6 People's Courts shall, on a quarterly basis, conduct a summary and analysis of the content in the dedicated database for information on inquiries by external persons that involves inquiries by leading cadres, and submit it to the Political and Legal Affairs Committee of the relevant Party committee and the People's Court at the next higher level. Where the recorded content involves leading cadres at the same level of the Party committee or the main leading cadres of the Political and Legal Affairs Committee of the Party committee, it shall be submitted to the Political and Legal Affairs Committee of the Party committee at the next higher level and the People's Court at the next higher level. Where a People's Court considers that a leading cadre's interference in judicial activities or intervention in the handling of a specific case is serious and may cause a wrongful conviction or other serious consequences, it shall immediately report the matter and submit it level by level to the Supreme People's Court.

Each High People's Court shall strengthen supervision and inspection of the implementation of the Provisions within its jurisdiction, promptly report the implementation status of the Provisions and these Measures to the Supreme People's Court, and submit a report to the Political and Legal Affairs Committee of the Party committee of the relevant province, autonomous region, or municipality directly under the Central Government once every six months.

Article 7 When reporting on external inquiries into cases, People's Courts shall list the following acts by leading cadres as special reporting items:

(1) Entreating, or making pleas, on behalf of a party to a case during the trial or enforcement stages;
(2) Requiring personnel of the People's Court to privately meet or contact a party to a case, or the party's defender, agent ad litem, close relative, or other person with an interest in the case;
(3) Instructing or condoning working staff or relatives to entreat or make pleas on behalf of a party to a case;
(4) Exceeding their authority to express a tendentious opinion or specific requirement on the handling of a case, by means such as hearing reports, convening coordination meetings, issuing documents, or making phone calls;
(5) Requiring the People's Court to docket a case, not to docket a case, to delay docketing, or to artificially control docketing;
(6) Requiring the People's Court to take measures such as suspending the trial, extending the trial period, or excluding periods from the trial period to delay case conclusion, or to compress the trial time to conclude the case;
(7) Requiring the People's Court to take, suspend, or lift the seizure, impoundment, or freezing of the subject property of preservation or the subject property of enforcement;
(8) Requiring the People's Court to select a specific appraisal institution, asset evaluation institution, auction institution, or administrator of the property of a bankrupt enterprise;
(9) Requiring the People's Court to prioritize the distribution of enforcement funds to a specific applying party for enforcement;
(10) Requiring the People's Court to delay enforcement of a case or to handle it by suspending enforcement or terminating enforcement;
(11) Requiring the People's Court to return property involved in a criminal case to a specific victim or to transfer it to a specific organ;
(12) Requiring the People's Court to take compulsory measures against a party, or to lift or alter compulsory measures against a party who has been lawfully subjected to compulsory measures;
(13) Requiring the People's Court to impose a stricter or more lenient sentence on a criminal during the trial of a commutation or parole case;
(14) Forwarding case materials or expert opinions unilaterally submitted by a party to a case, or the party's defender, agent ad litem, close relative, or other person with an interest in the case;
(15) Other acts that should be reported as special reporting items.

Article 8 Where a personnel member of a People's Court fails to record, or fails to truthfully record, a leading cadre's interference in judicial activities or intervention in the handling of a specific case, they shall be given a warning or a notice of criticism. Where there are two or more instances of failure to record or to truthfully record, disciplinary action shall be imposed in accordance with Article 54 of the "Regulations on Sanctions for Personnel of the People's Courts." Where the supervising leader instructs a subordinate not to record or not to truthfully record, disciplinary action shall be imposed in accordance with Article 76 of the "Regulations on Sanctions for Personnel of the People's Courts."

Article 9 Where a personnel member of a People's Court, due to strict compliance with the Provisions and these Measures, faces harassment, retaliation, or reprisal from a specific organization or individual in areas such as assessment, promotion, or performance of duties, they may file a complaint with the People's Court at the next higher level. The relevant People's Court shall promptly report the matter to the Political and Legal Affairs Committee of the Party committee at the same level, and may, if necessary, submit the report level by level to the Supreme People's Court.

Article 10 The term "leading cadres" as used in these Measures refers to leading cadres who hold the status of state functionaries in Party organs, People's Congress organs, administrative organs, Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference organs, procuratorial organs, military organs, as well as in companies, enterprises, public institutions, and social organizations, including retired leading cadres.

The term "personnel of the People's Court" as used in these Measures refers to personnel of People's Courts at all levels who lawfully perform adjudicative, adjudicative support, or judicial administrative functions, who are on the regular staff and are not workers or service personnel. Personnel employed by the People's Court on a contractual basis shall be handled by reference to these Provisions.

Where leading cadres of the People's Court inquire about cases, seek information on case details, or entreat or make pleas on behalf of others, the "Provisions on the Recording and Accountability for Internal Personnel of Judicial Organs Inquiring About Cases" and its implementation measures shall apply.

Article 11 The interpretation of these Measures rests with the Supreme People's Court. High People's Courts may formulate implementation rules in accordance with these Measures and submit them to the Supreme People's Court for filing.

Article 12 These Measures shall be implemented as of August 20, 2015.
